# Thistle's camp talks (story/camp_talk.gd): offered after a Long Rest once the opening `if` holds; each plays once.
# Quest: Grandda's Trail (narrative/companions/fen.dialogue). The file offers its first talk that holds: when she's
# Strained or Doubtful (story/approval.gd), those first; then the quest's; then Warm, Close and Devoted.

# --- When she's lost faith in the party (approval) ----------------------------------------------------------------

~ talk_strained
if name:thistle and approval.thistle <= strained
-> strained
endif
-> END

~ strained
Narrator: Thistle sleeps outside the firelight tonight, on her own, with her back to you. It's the first time she hasn't slept within arm's reach of somebody.
interject name:thistle: Not your pack tonight. Maybe not tomorrow.
interject name:thistle: A pack looks after its own and doesn't eat the little ones. That's all the rules. There's only two.
interject name:thistle: You keep breaking the second one.
interject name:thistle: I'm still going to Grandda. On my own if I have to. I'll not have you near him like this.
* Then show us what a pack does. -> strained_show
* We're sorry, Thistle. -> strained_sorry
* Go, then. -> strained_go

~ strained_show
interject name:thistle: Easy. Little ones behind you. You eat last. You don't leave nobody. Do that.
interject name:thistle: Do that, and I'll come back to the fire.
approve thistle +10: You asked me to show you what a pack does
-> END

~ strained_sorry
interject name:thistle: Sorry's a word. Words don't smell like anything. Show me.
approve thistle +5: You told me you were sorry
-> END

~ strained_go
Narrator: She doesn't answer. In the morning she's still with you, but a little farther off, the way a dog walks when it's been kicked and hasn't decided yet.
approve thistle -6: You told me to go
-> END

~ talk_doubt
if name:thistle and approval.thistle == doubtful
-> doubt
endif
-> END

~ doubt
Narrator: Thistle isn't up a tree tonight. She's on the ground, right across the fire, staring at you. She's been doing it for some time.
interject name:thistle: You smell wrong. Lately. All of you. Like a dog that's been in the bins.
interject name:thistle: Grandda says you can tell a pack by what it leaves behind. We've been leaving bad things.
if flag.den_children_left
interject name:thistle: Pups. In the den. We left the pups.
endif
interject name:thistle: Fix it. Or don't. But I'm watching.
* You're right. We'll fix it. -> doubt_fix
* What would you have done, Thistle? -> doubt_ask
* Stop sniffing us. -> doubt_sniff

~ doubt_fix
interject name:thistle: Good. Then I'll stop staring. Mostly.
approve thistle +6: You said we'd fix it
-> END

~ doubt_ask
interject name:thistle: Bit them. Then gone and got the little ones out. Then had supper. It's not hard. You lot make it hard.
approve thistle +3: You asked me what I'd have done
-> END

~ doubt_sniff
interject name:thistle: Can't. Nose works. Yours should.
approve thistle -4: You told me to stop sniffing you
-> END

# --- Her quest ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

~ talk_grandda
if name:thistle and quest.fens_trail
-> grandda
endif
-> END

~ grandda
Narrator: Thistle isn't in her bedroll. She's up a tree at the edge of the firelight, straddling a branch, eating something she caught.
interject name:thistle: Can't sleep on the ground here. Ground's wrong. Smells like a cellar.
* Tell us about your grandda. -> grandda_tell
* What are you eating? -> grandda_eat

~ grandda_eat
interject name:thistle: Don't know. It had legs. Want some?
-> grandda_tell

~ grandda_tell
interject name:thistle: Fen. Fen Burley. Not my real grandda; he found me in a fox's den when I was this big. Said the vixen didn't want me and he didn't either, but somebody had to.
interject name:thistle: He doesn't talk. Not much. I learned talking from him, so that's why I'm like this. He says one word when ten would do and then he goes and does the thing.
interject name:thistle: He taught me tracking. Traps. Which mushrooms. How to sit still for a whole day for a deer. How to... how to do the hares quick, so they don't feel it.
interject name:thistle: He went after that wolf because it took the dogs. Old Bess and Nettle. He loved those dogs. He never said. He went after them anyway.
interject name:thistle: I'll find him. I can track a moth across a frozen lake. I'll find him.
* We'll help. -> grandda_help
* What if he's... -> grandda_dead

~ grandda_help
interject name:thistle: Course you will. You're my pack now. That's how packs work.
approve thistle +2: You said you'd help me find Grandda
-> END

~ grandda_dead
interject name:thistle: Then I'll find that. And I'll bury him proper. And then I'll find the wolf.
Narrator: She goes back to eating whatever it was. You don't think she's hungry.
-> END

~ talk_towns
if name:thistle and visited:vallaki and flag.eva_truth_teller != "thistle"
-> towns
endif
-> END

~ towns
Narrator: Thistle comes back to camp late, very pleased with herself, with powdered sugar all down her front.
interject name:thistle: Don't say anything.
* Is that sugar? -> towns_sugar
* We won't. -> towns_sugar

~ towns_sugar
interject name:thistle: It's from the town. There's a woman sells little cakes. Little round ones, with jam in. I had six.
interject name:thistle: I hate towns. Stone boxes. Everybody whispering. Nobody says what they mean. You can't see the sky.
interject name:thistle: The cakes are all right.
interject name:thistle: And the beds. The beds at the inn are all right. And the fire in the big room, with everyone round it, and the singing. That's all right.
interject name:thistle: Don't tell Grandda. He'd say I'd gone soft. Like a house cat.
if name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: There's nothing wrong with a house cat. House cats are brilliant. They live in houses AND they can kill things.
endif
if name:liriel_dawnsong
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: You can belong to the woods and the town both, dear heart. Most of us belong to more than one place. It's how we know we're not lost.
endif
interject name:thistle: Six cakes. I'm getting more tomorrow.
approve thistle +1: You didn't laugh about the cakes
-> END

~ talk_after
if name:thistle and flag.fen_fate
-> after
endif
-> END

~ after
if flag.fen_fate == "cured"
Narrator: Thistle is braiding crow feathers into a cord in the firelight, fast and neat, and humming something tuneless and happy under her breath.
interject name:thistle: It's for Grandda. For when we go to Krezk. He likes things with feathers. He'll pretend he doesn't.
interject name:thistle: He's old now. He was old before, but he's old now. All that wolf went out of him and left an old man. He kept patting my face, like he couldn't believe it was there.
interject name:thistle: Thank you. For the... the prayer. For that. I don't say thank you right. Grandda says I say it like a threat. THANK YOU.
elif flag.fen_fate == "freed"
Narrator: Somewhere far off in the hills a single wolf howls, long and low, and stops. Thistle, at the fire, lifts her head.
interject name:thistle: That's him. That's Grandda. He's saying goodnight.
interject name:thistle: He'll be all right up there. The high woods are wide. He won't hunt kids. He'll hunt deer and the odd stupid shepherd and he'll be all right.
interject name:thistle: Every full moon, I'll know where he is. That's something. That's more than most people get.
Narrator: She cups her hands and howls back. It's a very good howl. Nobody in camp sleeps for a while after it.
else
Narrator: Thistle hasn't spoken all day. Tonight she sits by the fire with her knees up and her knife in her hands, cleaning a blade that is already clean.
interject name:thistle: He wasn't scared. Did you see? He wasn't scared. He was looking at me the whole time.
interject name:thistle: He taught me that. The quick way. For hares. So they don't feel it. I didn't know what he was teaching me. I thought it was hares.
interject name:thistle: Good lass. That's what he said. Good lass.
Narrator: Somebody sits down next to her. She leans on them, hard, and doesn't say anything else, and that's all right.
endif
-> END

# --- As she comes to trust the party (approval) -------------------------------------------------------------------

~ talk_warm
if name:thistle and approval.thistle >= warm and level >= 3
-> warm
endif
-> END

~ warm
Narrator: Thistle drops out of a tree beside you with no warning at all, which she seems to think is a greeting.
interject name:thistle: You. Arm-wrestle. Now. Big's asleep and I need to win something.
* (Arm-wrestle her.) -> warm_wrestle
* (Let her win.) -> warm_letwin
* Not tonight, Thistle. -> warm_no

~ warm_wrestle
check Strength DC 15 -> warm_won | warm_lost

~ warm_won
Narrator: It takes a long time and both your faces go red, but her knuckles touch the log first.
interject name:thistle: BARK AND BONES. Again! No. Tomorrow. My arm's gone. You're all right, you. You're pack.
approve thistle +3: You beat me at arm-wrestling, fair and square
-> END

~ warm_lost
Narrator: Your knuckles hit the log hard enough to hurt. She whoops loud enough to wake the camp.
interject name:thistle: Ha! Good try. Proper try. You didn't let me. I'd have smelled it.
approve thistle +3: You arm-wrestled me properly and didn't let me win
-> END

~ warm_letwin
Narrator: You go easy. She stops pushing at once and looks at you, deeply offended.
interject name:thistle: You let me. Don't let me. Grandda never let me, not once. That's how I knew he thought I was real.
approve thistle -1: You let me win at arm-wrestling
-> END

~ warm_no
interject name:thistle: Fine. Tomorrow. I'm going to be so strong tomorrow.
-> END

~ talk_close
if name:thistle and approval.thistle >= close and level >= 5
-> close
endif
-> END

~ close
Narrator: Thistle is lying on her back by the fire, looking up at the place where stars would be if the fog let them through.
interject name:thistle: In the Thornwood you can see all of them. Grandda knows the names. Not the real names. His names. That one's the Old Hare. That one's Bess's Nose.
interject name:thistle: When we've got Grandda, I'm going home. To the Thornwood. That's the plan.
interject name:thistle: Only I never had a pack that talks back before. Never had folk to sit by that weren't him and the dogs. And I'm going to miss you. I'm going to miss you so much I'm angry about it.
* Then come and find us, after. -> close_find
* The Thornwood's lucky to have you. -> close_lucky
* We'll miss you too. -> close_miss

~ close_find
interject name:thistle: I can do that. I can find anybody. I can track a moth across a frozen lake. You'll never get rid of me.
approve thistle +3: You told me to come and find you, after
-> close_end

~ close_lucky
interject name:thistle: It is. It doesn't know it. Trees never know anything. That's why you have to tell them things.
approve thistle +2: You told me the Thornwood's lucky to have me
-> close_end

~ close_miss
interject name:thistle: Good. You should. I'm very good to have about.
approve thistle +3: You told me you'll miss me too
-> close_end

~ close_end
interject name:thistle: Don't tell Big I said any of that. He'll cry. He cries at everything.
interject name:thistle: I'm not crying. It's the smoke.
-> END

~ talk_devoted
if name:thistle and approval.thistle >= devoted and level >= 8
-> devoted
endif
-> END

~ devoted
Narrator: The fog thins for once after midnight, and for a few minutes there are stars over the camp. Thistle wakes everyone to see them, whether they want to or not.
interject name:thistle: LOOK. Look. There's the Old Hare. There's Bess's Nose.
interject name:thistle: And that one. The little one by the Hare, see? That's new. I'm naming it.
* What's it called? -> devoted_name
* (Just look.) -> devoted_name

~ devoted_name
interject name:thistle: The Pack. ...It's a rubbish name. It's the best name. It's all of you.
interject name:thistle: When I'm home and you're wherever, I'll look up and there you'll be. Being rubbish. Being mine.
approve thistle +3: You let me name a star for us
inspire name:thistle: named a star for her pack
-> END
